#
# Counter-example for math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape (Rule P2): a node typed BOTH
# math:ProbabilityValue AND math:OddsValue. Odds are a probability-scale transform held
# owl:disjointWith the closed unit interval, so the sh:not [ sh:class math:OddsValue ]
# fires — shacl.NotConstraintComponent (math:ProbabilityScaleConflation).
# Single violation: it carries a gmeow:hasReferenceFrame so math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape
# (P3) stays SATISFIED, it carries NO math:quantityValue so the range gate
# math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape (P1) is vacuously satisfied, and NO logic:confidence so
# math:ConfidenceAsProbabilityConstraint (P10) stays silent — EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling fires.
# Back-reference: math:OddsValue owl:disjointWith math:ProbabilityValue / math:ProbabilityScaleConflation (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilityScaleConflationBad).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:conflatedScale a math:ProbabilityValue , math:OddsValue ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:forecastFrame .

ex:forecastFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/conflatedScale> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
